{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Calibration — {{ a.display_name }}{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<article class="prose">
<h1>Calibration</h1>
<p>For every market that resolved, we look at the YES price 24 hours before settlement (from our own snapshots) and compare it with the outcome. A perfectly calibrated venue resolves YES 70% of the time when priced at 70¢. Brier score: lower is better (0 = perfect, 0.25 = coin flip).</p>
<p>Resolved markets with a 24h-before price: <b>{{ n_all }}</b> (last 7 days: {{ n_week }}).</p>
<h2>Running Brier score by venue</h2>
<table><tr><th>Venue</th><th>n</th><th>Brier</th></tr>
{% for v in venues %}<tr><td>{{ v.name }}</td><td>{{ v.n }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f' % v.brier if v.brier is not none else '—' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<h2>Reliability table (all time)</h2>
<table><tr><th>Priced (24h before)</th><th>n</th><th>Resolved YES</th><th>Rate</th></tr>
{% for b in buckets %}<tr><td>{{ b.bucket }}</td><td>{{ b.n }}</td><td>{{ b.yes }}</td><td>{{ '%.0f%%' % (b.rate*100) if b.rate is not none else '—' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<p>Raw ledger: <a href="/data/resolutions.csv">resolutions.csv</a> (last 90 days, CC BY 4.0).
The numbers above use the full ledger. Download the full history from the
<a href="https://github.com/{{ a.repo }}">repo</a>.</p>
</article>
{% endblock %}
